I have a MUCH better solution for leprechauns than stairs or dropping
gold on the ground. (If you have gold under your feet, they can snatch
it and teleport away.) 

I call it the old "Here; hold this while I thrash you." method. 

I throw them all my gold, which they catch, but do not teleport. Then
I thrash them, as I no longer have anything that makes them teleport.
It works like a charm. If I had something to keep my gold in, I'd use
that, but this is sometimes more fun. (for me. The leprechauns don't
get much out of it besides cold steel...)

Lots of times, I just treat the leprechaun level like a bank -- I
don't clean it out until I need $$$. Kind of like leaving a spellbook
in an armor shop. (They don't give you anything for it, but nobody
takes it, either.)



